# Keys this base needs. Copy to .env and fill in; never commit the filled-in .env.
#
# Model key for OpenClaw (Claudia's reasoning) and your build agent:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   recommended (the course defaults Claudia to a Claude model).
#   OPENAI_API_KEY      if you run Claudia or your coding agent on an OpenAI model instead.
#   At least one of these must be set. OpenAI-compatible providers (DeepSeek, OpenRouter)
#   also set OPENAI_BASE_URL.
#
# PAPERCLIP_API_KEY   the key the paperclip MCP server boots with. Note the split: the
#   LOCAL-TRUSTED sandbox HTTP server (paperclipai onboard --yes, default loopback) needs
#   no auth on its routes, but the @paperclipai/mcp-server CLIENT refuses to start without
#   a non-empty PAPERCLIP_API_KEY. So the sandbox path uses a placeholder the sandbox never
#   validates: the .mcp.json / opencode.json ship PAPERCLIP_API_KEY=local-trusted for exactly
#   this. Set a real key here ONLY for bring-your-own (your OWN deployed Paperclip), minted
#   via `paperclipai agent local-cli`; for the sandbox the shipped placeholder is enough.
#
# DATABASE_URL   the governance_ledger Postgres. You do not fill this by hand: the agent
#   provisions Neon over the Neon MCP, then writes DATABASE_URL here at build time.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
PAPERCLIP_API_KEY=
